CronJob


CronJob

For scheduled jobs.

Equivalent of Linux cron.

Example:

	Run backup every midnight


CronJob Example


apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob

metadata:
  name: backup-job

spec:
  schedule: "0 0 * * *"

  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          containers:
            - name: backup

              image: busybox

              command:
                - sh
                - -c
                - echo "Running backup"

          restartPolicy: OnFailure


Deployment vs Job vs CronJob

Resource			Purpose

Deployment			Always-running apps
Job	One-time 		task
CronJob				Scheduled repeated task


1. Create CronJob YAML
cronjob.yaml
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob

metadata:
  name: backup-cronjob

spec:
  schedule: "*/1 * * * *"

  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:

          containers:
            - name: backup

              image: busybox

              command:
                - sh
                - -c
                - date; echo "Backup Running"

          restartPolicy: OnFailure



2. Apply CronJob

	kubectl apply -f cronjob.yaml


3. List CronJobs

	kubectl get cronjobs

Short form:

kubectl get cj

4. Describe CronJob

kubectl describe cronjob backup-cronjob

5. Check Jobs Created By CronJob

kubectl get jobs

6. Check Pods Created

kubectl get pods

7. View Logs

	Get Pod Name

	kubectl get pods

Then:

	kubectl logs <pod-name>

OR directly:

	kubectl logs job/<job-name>

8. Delete CronJob

	kubectl delete cronjob backup-cronjob

Short form:

	kubectl delete cj backup-cronjob

9. Suspend CronJob

Pause schedule execution:

	kubectl patch cronjob backup-cronjob \
-p '{"spec":{"suspend":true}}'


10. Resume CronJob

kubectl patch cronjob backup-cronjob \
-p '{"spec":{"suspend":false}}'


11. Run CronJob Immediately (Manual Trigger)

Create Job from CronJob:

kubectl create job manual-job \
--from=cronjob/backup-cronjob


12. Delete Jobs

kubectl delete job <job-name>

Delete all jobs:

kubectl delete jobs --all

13. Watch CronJob Execution

kubectl get pods -w

14. Watch Jobs

kubectl get jobs -w

15. Edit CronJob

	kubectl edit cronjob backup-cronjob

16. Get YAML
	
	kubectl get cronjob backup-cronjob -o yaml

17. Export YAML
	
	kubectl get cronjob backup-cronjob -o yaml > cronjob.yaml

18. Check Events

	kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp

Common Cron Schedules

Schedule	Meaning

"* * * * *"	every minute
"*/5 * * * *"	every 5 minutes
"0 * * * *"	every hour
"0 0 * * *"	every midnight
"0 9 * * 1"	every Monday 9 AM